per wikihack, the chance of finding a trap using #untrap
depends purely on experience level, starting just over 1/3
at Xlvl 1 and going to 100% at Xlvl 21. But there's no chance
of setting one of by #untrap, so you may as well do it a few
times before trying to open the chest.

Again per wikihack, your chance to disarm the trap
depends on your level and dexterity, dungeon level, and
whether you're a rogue, but it isn't good. [If I'm reading
the formula correctly, it's (Dex + xlvl)/(75+ dlvl/2), double
for rogues.]

Luck affects the chance that the trap is harmless and also
how bad it is, though one of the less bad traps will paralyze
you for 5d6 turns which seems like enough time for
something to mess you up bad. Reading this spoiler has
made me think I should be #untrapping chests a lot more.

